Package: InsideProcess
Type: Package
Title: Validity Evidence Based on Response Processes from Cognitive Interviews
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jose", "Ventura-Leon",
                   email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
                   role = c("aut", "cre"),
                   comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
Description: Gathers and quantifies validity evidence based on response
    processes (Padilla and Benitez, 2014 <doi:10.7334/psicothema2013.259>)
    through self-administered cognitive interviews (web probing). It writes a
    ready-to-use web form, either as a 'Google Apps Script' web application
    that stores every answer and the seconds spent on each item in a 'Google
    Sheets' spreadsheet, or as a script that builds a native 'Google Forms'
    questionnaire. Probes follow the four stages of the survey response model
    of Tourangeau, Rips and Rasinski (2000) <doi:10.1017/CBO9780511819322>:
    comprehension (clarity rating, paraphrase, confusing words), retrieval,
    judgment and response. Open answers of each stage are coded with a
    common scheme (adequate, partial, inadequate, not assessable) and turned
    into item-level metrics: comprehension index, problem index with a
    Wilson (1927) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1927.10502953> interval, problems in
    each stage, severity, discordance between declared and shown
    understanding, use of the answer options, and a keep, revise or
    reformulate decision. Intercoder agreement is given for each stage
    with Cohen's kappa and the AC1 coefficient of Gwet (2008)
    <doi:10.1348/000711006X126600>, together with sensitivity analyses without
    doubtful participants, response quality per participant, tables and
    figures. Functions are standalone: there is no pipeline to follow.
